WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.610
John Betjeman's poem Slough asks for
friendly bombs to fall on the town.

2
00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:09.710
In 2002, another area's
MP told Parliament:

3
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.690
I would not be as unkind as Mr Betjeman.

4
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:16.690
The same speech used the
town as a unit of sprawl:

5
00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.050
40 towns the size of Slough.

6
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:24.770
In 2019, Slough's own MP answered
back: Slough is on the up.

7
00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:28.430
Can a poem really shape the way
a town is seen, and treated?

8
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:31.370
Or is it only a poem?

9
00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:36.390
In this mission, you'll set poems
and TV comedy beside census tables.

10
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:40.770
Then you'll see how who you
are changes how a place feels.

11
00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:45.640
Your mission: decide whether a poem
can shape how a real place is treated.
